# How to keep chilling when your codebase is big

## 1. Do EDD (Error Driven Development)

{pause}
- Navigate the codebase with errors.

{.example #codingclick}
> Coding the "click-to-source" feature.
>
> - **Plan mode?** The engine has to send a message to the editor with the
>   location. This message has to go through the preview server I think and hmm the previewer and what on earth is a synchronizer? **High cognitive load!** {pause}
>
>  {#exmode}
> - **Execution mode**:
>
>   - Me:
>     ```diff
>     type preview_communication =
>       | Ready
>       | Go_forward
>     + | Goto_location of loc
>     ```
>     {pause up=exmode}
>   - The compiler:
>     ```
>     File "slipshow/src/engine/runtime/controller.ml", lines 230-272, characters 6-12:
>     File "slipshow/src/engine/previewer/previewer.ml", lines 142-175, characters 10-16:
>     Error (warning 8 [partial-match]): this pattern-matching is not exhaustive.
>     ```
>     {pause}
>   - Me:
>     ```diff
>     - let create_previewer = function
>     + let create_previewer ~goto_loc = function
>     +| Goto_location loc -> goto_loc loc
>     ```
>     {pause down=nextone}
>   - The compiler:
>
>     {#nextone}
>     ```
>     File "slipshow/src/server/client/client.ml", line 146, characters 27-37:
>     Error: The value previewer has type loc -> blabla
>       but an expression was expected of type Previewer.previewer
>     ```
>     {pause down=nextnextone}
>   - Me:
>
>     {#nextnextone}
>     ```diff
>     type lsp_communication =
>       | Ready
>     + | Goto_loc of loc
>
>     - let previewer = create_previewer ev in
>     + let goto_loc = send Goto_loc
>     + let previewer = create_previewer ~goto_loc ev in
>     + let create_previewer ~callback_goto_loc = function
>     +   | Goto_location loc -> goto_loc loc
>     ```
>     {pause down=nextnextnextone}
>   - The compiler:
>
>     {#nextnextnextone}
>     ```
>     File "slipshow/src/server/server.ml", lines 176-205, characters 10-54:
>     Error (warning 8 [partial-match]): this pattern-matching is not exhaustive.
>     ```
>   - ... {pause down=codingclick } Until the feature is implemented

{up=smap}

{pause up}
- Introduce errors wherever possible.

{.example}
> {carousel change-page=~n:all}
> ------
> {.flex}
> ----
> ```ocaml
> (* parsing.ml.
>    Shared between
>    compiler and engine *)
>
>                           
>
> module type S = sig
> 
>   ...
> end
>
> module Action1 : S = ...
>
> module Action2 : S = ...
>
> module Action3 : S = ...
> ```
> ---
> ```ocaml
> (* execution.ml
>
>    Engine only. *)
>
>                                            
>
> module type S = sig
> 
>   ...
> end
>
> module Action1 : S = ...
>
> module Action2 : S = ...
>
> module Action3 : S = ...
> ```
> -----
> {.flex}
> ----
> ```ocaml
> (* parsing.ml.
>    Shared between
>    compiler and engine *)
>
> type t = Action1 | Action2
>
> module type S = sig
>   val repr : t
>   ...
> end
>
> module Action1 : S = ...
>
> module Action2 : S = ...
>
> module Action3 : S = ...
> ```
> ---
> ```ocaml
> (* execution.ml
>
>    Engine only. *)
>
> type t = Parsing.action = Action1 | Action2
>
> module type S = sig
>   val repr : t
>   ...
> end
>
> module Action1 : S = ...
>
> module Action2 : S = ...
>
> module Action3 : S = ...
> ```

{pause center}
- Leave artificial errors for your future self.

{.example}
> {.flex}
> ----
> ![](wip.png){width=100%}
> ---
> ```
> File "slipshow/src/server/server.ml",
> lines 176-205, characters 10-54:
> Error: Unbound value implement_me
> ```

{pause up}
## 2. Celebrate the extensive set of OCaml features

- **GADTs for a nice action parsing API**

```ocaml
type 'a argument =
  string * (string -> 'a)

type _ input =
  | [] : unit input
  | ( :: ) : 'a argument * 'b input -> ('a * 'b) input

type _ output =
  | [] : unit output
  | ( :: ) : 'a option * 'b output -> ('a * 'b) output

val parse : action_name:string -> 'named input -> string -> 'named output
```

{pause down="~margin:50 sblock"}
- **Extensible variants for extending `cmarkit`'s AST**

{#sblock}
```ocaml
type s_block =
  | Slide of slide attributed node
  | Slip of Block.t attributed node
  | SlipScript of Block.Code_block.t attributed node

type Block.t += S_block of s_block

```

{pause down="~margin:50 all_actions"}
- **First-class modules for putting action modules in a list**

{#all_actions}
```ocaml
let all_actions =
  [
    (module Enter : S);
    (module Clear_draw : S);
    (module Draw : S);
    (module Pause : S);
    [...];
    (module Play_media : S);
  ]
```

{pause down="~margin:50 objects"}
- **Objects for extending a base LSP server**

{#objects}
```ocaml
    method! config_completion =
      Some (CompletionOptions.create ~triggerCharacters:[ "#" ] ())
```

{pause down="~margin:50 operators"}
- **Operators for satisfying eDSL design**

{#operators}
```ocaml
val ( ||| ) :
    Slipshow.file_reader -> Slipshow.file_reader -> Slipshow.file_reader

let read_file =
  Read_file.with_ file source
  ||| read_from_buffer parent
  ||| Fs.read_file in
```

{pause down="~margin:50 letops"}
- **Let-operators for improving the readability**

{#letops}
```ocaml
let (let*) x f =
  let open Fut.Syntax in
  let* x, undo1 = x in
  let* y, undo2 = f x in
  let undo () =
    let* () = undo2 () in
    undo1 ()
  in
  Fut.return (y, undo)
```

{pause down="~margin:50 interopoint"}
- **Effects and multicore although I don't use them yet... one day...**

{#interopoint}
```ocaml
????
```

{pause up}
## Use the excellent ecosystem of OCaml libraries

Thanks!!!

- **LSP:**

  - `linol` for being an LSP IKEA 🤗

- **Build:**

  - `dune` for handling the complex build of slipshow easily 🙏

- **Compiler:**

  - `cmdliner` for making top-class CLI easy

  - `cmarkit` for allowing me to extend its AST 🤗

  - `grace` for making top-class error reporting easy 🙏

  - `dream` for being a simple server 🙏

- **Engine:**

  - `js_of_ocaml` for bringing OCaml everywhere

  - `brr` for bringing OCaml everywhere 🤗

  - `lwd` for unlocking UI programming 🤗

-----

